From: WebKit Symbian port
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve 28-bit descriptors and validate file IPC buffers

Symbian descriptor length occupies bits 0..27, not 0..23. The old
file server copied the truncated length but wrote the separately supplied
full request length, reading past the host buffer and hiding short writes.

Validate guest descriptor headers and the entire payload range, then use
bounded page-aware transfers which also support noncontiguous host pages.
Reject invalid lengths/offsets, propagate failed writes, and handle read
EOF without unsigned underflow. Position writes beyond EOF at EOF, as RFile
specifies; POSIX gap extension belongs to OpenC before RFile::Write.

